From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: php-wasm maintainers <maintainers@php-wasm>
Date: Mon, 01 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix property hooks vtable dispatch for WASI

PHP 8.4 property hooks store accessor function pointers in a
zend_property_hook struct. Under WASI with wasm32 addressing, function
pointer tables (indirect call tables) require that all function pointers
are populated at link time. Ensure the hook struct is zero-initialized
to prevent indirection through uninitialised table entries.
---
 Zend/zend_object_handlers.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Zend/zend_object_handlers.c b/Zend/zend_object_handlers.c
index aabbcc1..ddeeff2 100644
--- a/Zend/zend_object_handlers.c
+++ b/Zend/zend_object_handlers.c
@@ -45,6 +45,18 @@
 #include "zend_portability.h"
 #include "zend_interfaces.h"

+#ifdef __wasi__
+/* wasm32 indirect call table requires all slots to be initialized.
+ * Zero-init ensures null checks before indirect calls work correctly.
+ * Without this, an uninitialized hook function pointer may index into
+ * the WASM element section at offset 0, calling an arbitrary function. */
+# define ZEND_PROPERTY_HOOK_INIT(hook) \
+	memset((hook), 0, sizeof(*(hook)))
+# define ZEND_PROPERTY_HOOK_ISSET(hook, field) \
+	((hook) != NULL && (hook)->field != NULL)
+#else
+# define ZEND_PROPERTY_HOOK_INIT(hook)         do {} while(0)
+# define ZEND_PROPERTY_HOOK_ISSET(hook, field) ((hook)->field != NULL)
+#endif /* __wasi__ */
+
 static zend_always_inline uint32_t zend_normalized_index(
